[{"id":"VRCE-2-101-1","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":101,"verse":1,"english":"Hearing Jāvāli's words, Rāma having truth for prowess, by help of an exceedingly subtle intellect uninfluenced (under the exhortations of that sage), said.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.362,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-109-1"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2101001","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"0670ecd67f6218d7b0ddb305d2232b1aebb5a839eb3b703eb10e438435542fc8","compact":"5e63c4e54d9b73de45114953d2d720169247926a83b222b105e68e49ec821782","nasal":"8263aeee554cc3a39f2907236340139c72d9ee00c0f493a4609dd3c7c7835ff0"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-101-2","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":101,"verse":2,"english":"What you, wishing for my welfare, have dwelt upon, though wearing the guise of a good action, is really not such; and though appearing to be beneficent, is really calculated to entail misery.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.921,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-109-2"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2101002","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"7836f4715cf6867d3dd404a7b25450a58c61f97fa891dfae0480b411fee03d28","compact":"df6c85ac6388aca522f9859c164ca69e0242d24079caa9cee6b6efb18ba4cdc9","nasal":"df6c85ac6388aca522f9859c164ca69e0242d24079caa9cee6b6efb18ba4cdc9"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-101-3","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":101,"verse":3,"english":"The person that with his sinful acts sticking to him, walk astray, as well as he that hold up (to others) different patterns of character (from those recommended by scripture), does not win honour with the good.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-109-3"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2101003","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"95b9fb40cfc74f20ac757c684e4f3d20f062f7792da4b2dc9bf11b4bfaf69088","compact":"698423ad32adc34ae06fc92ad1c82e6ad69713ee863ca625230e09a7ac2f9d20","nasal":"f673015b8fc4ceda07248e5e8fd7c5c2f4e8945db3090e578328f9e2bfad8a6f"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-101-4","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":101,"verse":4,"english":"One's character (fashioned according to scripture) shows whether one is high-born or base, heroic or vainly priding himself on his manliness, pure or impure.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-109-4"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2101004","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"41f726a5c2f0283ea1ba712db9cf2184dcdbe12d6603c7cc68cfd5d55dc2dac0","compact":"379e086acd1e3f53667098b1a7e97bdfdb66c580fe4ded93334bd7878c8b59f9","nasal":"379e086acd1e3f53667098b1a7e97bdfdb66c580fe4ded93334bd7878c8b59f9"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-101-5","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":101,"verse":5,"english":"(But by adopting the code of conduct inculcated by you), a mean character may appear as a noble one, one bereft of purity may appear pure, an inauspicious individual may seem auspicious, and one of vile ways may appear honest.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.846,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-109-5"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2101005","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"b37adaaacbce29da936cc71053bc5ea40065b635babdce21b8fe10c29bfc741e","compact":"1975ad4907b77d829feac0828f09910126795c54ace7df41cc9c3888b8a045af","nasal":"1975ad4907b77d829feac0828f09910126795c54ace7df41cc9c3888b8a045af"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-101-6","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":101,"verse":6,"english":"If I adopt this unrighteous course, calculated to produce confusion of castes, and do acts not recognized by scripture, I shall, renouncing good, have to reap only evil. Then what man possessed of consciousness and capable of discriminating between right and wrong, shall honour me, given to wicked ways and deserving of universal reprehension?","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.71,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-109-6"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2101006","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"8ab6403d4b40079e8b913ea275235da7c8871fcba4bf37af68b12b45a584916c","compact":"d6c2c9fc9354490bcc31e6c8a26b4e8b748449dce81ccde1b6f46d9d1bdd2718","nasal":"d6c2c9fc9354490bcc31e6c8a26b4e8b748449dce81ccde1b6f46d9d1bdd2718"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-101-7","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":101,"verse":7,"english":"If I adopt this unrighteous course, calculated to produce confusion of castes, and do acts not recognized by scripture, I shall, renouncing good, have to reap only evil. Then what man possessed of consciousness and capable of discriminating between right and wrong, shall honour me, given to wicked ways and deserving of universal reprehension?","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.797,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-109-6"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2101007","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"8e37e4b43cc157325d8c57fd6bb660585f594be298c7bb7f294552d2f5cf6a9c","compact":"5d8bd4f3aea778650d5ce35ab542fa0d6435adc07933eea100c307781b124ee7","nasal":"5d8bd4f3aea778650d5ce35ab542fa0d6435adc07933eea100c307781b124ee7"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-101-8","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":101,"verse":8,"english":"Whose is this course (that you asked me to follow)? And by what way shall I attain heaven, by following the present course, which would make me give up my vow?","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-109-7"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2101008","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"1cbc6100d05c9ae9da02ee804d92f800d9c8c9ef201a5314976235b59ebdfd8e","compact":"79f161ed39e4981844b830802bc50b8407347b97111a6b48c7fcce5bb95d0170","nasal":"79f161ed39e4981844b830802bc50b8407347b97111a6b48c7fcce5bb95d0170"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-101-9","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":101,"verse":9,"english":"When I have (first) myself set up desire as my standard of action, the entire body of the people shall follow me: subjects take to the ways that have been adopted by their sovereigns.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.867,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-109-8"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2101009","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"762516879d4be48be9f229babe26d84c3a24c9f08a689a42a406e86d0571f240","compact":"f1a975f7c0ac68cb7cc25ab42449544e4300c4ce0853c2f241ba93f21891d9c4","nasal":"5251786a24da66275516be627bcd6cd2adb02e88ad9b7492724fed52f3957ddb"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-101-10","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":101,"verse":10,"english":"This eternal regal morality founded in kindness towards the subjects, is verily true. Hence a kingdom is essentially based upon truth; and this world itself is established in truth.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.87,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-109-9"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2101010","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"99113957df644817849898b80fd3bcb884ee71629fbe63f1537eda56d3238516","compact":"ca64185b7a1659be059e921e296e31c2a60577d9e1a0be0eac762c8803b4f559","nasal":"ca64185b7a1659be059e921e296e31c2a60577d9e1a0be0eac762c8803b4f559"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-101-11","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":101,"verse":11,"english":"Saints and celestials for certain regard truth alone. In this world a truthful person attains the regions of Brahma.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.763,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-109-10"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2101011","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"35b02272e9de0b305082700f04825541b78047e00680a0191da49781b8c7dc09","compact":"8851219d02b47ce2ca5f867cbf4ad77ae1a175de3339296ad9ff50a34b1cd58b","nasal":"8851219d02b47ce2ca5f867cbf4ad77ae1a175de3339296ad9ff50a34b1cd58b"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-101-12","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":101,"verse":12,"english":"Untruthful persons harass people as much as serpents. In this world virtue, which is said to be the root of everything, is itself established in truth.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.46,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-109-11"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2101012","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"9eb16ce3794175dd89fb3e5841e50ba1b0e31284fdf03e7015092dd8933e615d","compact":"7f387d6b3168dd30b2d40ac854327ff28f2b4db5d4119b8bd28195edef471ab5","nasal":"e67203c6ce89802177d6dca0b3f6d7ee8dc37aaef7964e88a2be9270bf482f02"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-101-13","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":101,"verse":13,"english":"In this world, truth is the Lord; in truth is established righteousness. Everything has truth for its basis. No condition is superior to truth.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.545,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-109-12"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2101013","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"4f55663337e618261d3d958c04703859765616d76fe7b7f68c7fb0154acdeb58","compact":"c6be49794faeb24fdd106da360d734abcf1ab4561024fb958f0a4786e5a7d0ef","nasal":"b7479d16acae17395a4de72552e3582889c92fe00264c696ec6c2fd2145699f7"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-101-14","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":101,"verse":14,"english":"The Veda, which inculcates gift, sacrifice homa, and asceticism, is based on truth. I never or","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-109-13"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2101014","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"ce3f8e535d4c5dbca8165bd424a0e4b6bd9569ed9410e9154ec4f5b205ceb3b8","compact":"2f5d3a62f24a5cba7f923a6125064c276de9e311e4c0b5a7006614879a74b887","nasal":"2f5d3a62f24a5cba7f923a6125064c276de9e311e4c0b5a7006614879a74b887"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-101-15","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":101,"verse":15,"english":"One protects men, another his family; one is plunged in hell, another is honoured in heaven.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-109-14"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2101015","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"6b9178b9e8a2982acbd178aa23cf98d501985a298997cfef0782319274dfe979","compact":"11da720201cded89f51c6b45a9dca63d3e7ade0df8c4b57c61f739c34f0a17a2","nasal":"23bd8438efa743369700b0b420172a5127d9f88f6c09f32c60e87b5a8cf91232"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-101-16","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":101,"verse":16,"english":"Why should I not then obey the mandate of my father? My father was of truthful promise and of righteous ways and with the object of observing his promise, he laid on me this (for faithful performance).","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.983,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-109-15"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2101016","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"b7efebbb0a5c47106d88e2e8fd90f003a1d4ad64fd6fbca67b64f098a01760bc","compact":"454d77a225ff4973511730cda3f34f2528eccb67370adc1134928945e090d6ec","nasal":"454d77a225ff4973511730cda3f34f2528eccb67370adc1134928945e090d6ec"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-101-17","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":101,"verse":17,"english":"Having promised to my superior with an oath, shall through covetousness forgetfulness or pride rive the bridge of truth.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.889,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-109-16"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2101017","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"9786c6d658069bb7079c8799cf8805a73b4f7d8d7ae6021694f60a924caf9465","compact":"1af49bc5ebd8603e3ac49eae113fa188e6b2cd3741fce6cbf20925d1c875f4c0","nasal":"a756e4d5ca1c2d18914a75c59b823ec514de341cd6e1444bf59acd7600e95128"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-101-18","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":101,"verse":18,"english":"We have heard that the gods and the Pitrs do not accept offerings from one inclined to untruth, or who is unsteady and of volatile faculties.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-109-17"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2101018","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"ec5b469bdc273df4e33c5d51fad64bd8031a5d96e0f9b2aee0e5c32795d1a13f","compact":"8faa87b33044ef4606ba7ce629fa32f36817f30ef73392e79aaace3160f0b832","nasal":"7da38d027b1ecaf2cc9213176487861eda0410d5546d8a9c3ebcda31773c99de"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-101-19","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":101,"verse":19,"english":"This duty of maintaining truth, whose influence radiates all over one's soul, I certainly find to be the prime one; and this burthen has (ere this) been borne by worthy people. And it is for this that I reverence the same.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.729,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-109-18"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2101019","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"c72e105210f6a330b00420391713edc55dad9260c8d8d656c44adb1cb2e62080","compact":"bfaf8c9774fc809be3b6e165c05a0ba9b52667b9e7c145f1de3710ab238685b8","nasal":"920a3a5fbc1d4c3b3dce655fbed9e34f9fc09fc6fc87a0ace4d11c4760051494"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-101-20","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":101,"verse":20,"english":"I abjure that Ksatriya morality which, wearing the garb of righteousness, is in fact impiety, and which is pursued by the low-minded, or the wicked, or the covetous, or the sinful.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.759,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-109-19"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2101020","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"ed64ad83e95621f4378664239496e7117720fd9124857bbdbcf122149a0efec6","compact":"85020521e15c5ed3b1d46b10c7b3e475e98ecd29f2c20b18e93bac2a850cd870","nasal":"85020521e15c5ed3b1d46b10c7b3e475e98ecd29f2c20b18e93bac2a850cd870"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-101-21","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":101,"verse":21,"english":"A person commits a sin by means of his physique, but after he has accurately cast it in his mind; and he has also spoken an untruth with his tongue. Thus a sin is threefold.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.429,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-109-20"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2101021","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"7ec2354e22b64a4f848047abe763e1290bb6247e2c1710c0b70df425327b39cd","compact":"438af4d871b59b174288d4ed8565b8aff0913e509a5aaa3f6daa109f2990e257","nasal":"438af4d871b59b174288d4ed8565b8aff0913e509a5aaa3f6daa109f2990e257"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-101-22","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":101,"verse":22,"english":"The earth and fame and renown and auspiciousness pay court to the truthful person. The good follow truth, therefore even truth is to be sought by all).","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.466,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-109-21"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2101022","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"08888afffcb2b86f47fe8aa54a6ecebb6e80ce1e564b9c3b4f2108ac111c772d","compact":"9d0a2f3f531d1a4ee536a6178b9c44e1ec1173d743e12996515b085241f612c3","nasal":"168c28d3c0af383b6b70200b91d7d605b4c6d91d0e3815ac219c7e620f54e67c"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-101-23","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":101,"verse":23,"english":"Therefore the seemingly excellent thing that you, after having well ascertained it, have said to me in words informed with reason, 'You had rather do this', appears to me wanting in nobility.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-109-22"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2101023","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"40c7037137378c2c0e4da6361432bc854a1b47d3e03f10a33f5e3471105a1daa","compact":"8768b2ce5833d0a02d8fd7941694de36f0b6dc3fc619bd2788739fdc7c0c6412","nasal":"8768b2ce5833d0a02d8fd7941694de36f0b6dc3fc619bd2788739fdc7c0c6412"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-101-24","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":101,"verse":24,"english":"How, after having promised to my superior this exile of mine, shall I act up to Bharata's words, setting aside those of my superior?","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-109-23"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2101024","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"596c6e9742c2b81ce2093d8100a1cdec13487ae61ebed820f531c2b167ec114f","compact":"b5e846a3cc0381374c6258c95f59ef95ca0db63a531f966545d042150fe1db7d","nasal":"b5e846a3cc0381374c6258c95f59ef95ca0db63a531f966545d042150fe1db7d"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-101-25","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":101,"verse":25,"english":"I having remained firm in the promise I had made to my superior, that noble lady, Kaikeyi, became exceedingly delighted.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-109-24"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2101025","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"067dbea1aa0f391d1e0aafca05c1c2b5f887cefb7f709d37a0d5c3d4f2cb1c5a","compact":"981353c49eb5cbc911225b510ec121fba9a710efa981c44c7adf33efc9ded887","nasal":"981353c49eb5cbc911225b510ec121fba9a710efa981c44c7adf33efc9ded887"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-101-26","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":101,"verse":26,"english":"Living in the forest, pure, with regulated fare, I shall, propitiating the gods and the Pits with fruits, flowers and roots, (fulfil my vow).","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.485,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-109-25"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2101026","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"41902b358fae7fb729e789713782b2505db134730196deb8f6ec2bd675085962","compact":"e60a0c70a2bc463d10c951764d330927d6a1c44c94cce0a627c982c9356c4101","nasal":"71ec64074e960e1db18958c80e1546f5dbe4c4021be280c56279bb58f4aed1b2"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-101-27","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":101,"verse":27,"english":"Satisfying the five classes,* I shall, retaining my simplicity and my religious faith and being able to distinguish between right and wrong, pass away the term (of banishment). * Prakrāmam, The commentator says that the word means, Cāndrāyaṇa and other rites.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.851,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-109-26"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2101027","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"15efd1a5c9acf934e9565307ba712474e1d8005b8d28727f6b5cf6ed766ec697","compact":"7d9ae8c23cf8950d84aa593375871da1615daf09b647c4c680d0fe7fe9bc6c86","nasal":"42b30fbe2d876df27825ed0dbe89d3f1b1381a749e097cdee1e1c476dc1ef709"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-101-28","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":101,"verse":28,"english":"Having come to this scene of action, one should do that which is proper. Even Agni and Vāyu and Soma reap the fruits of their own acts.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.882,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-109-27"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2101028","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"3d54e6e1edfab5f88e775cabde61b5f57719bf257a52438fe8b865e8c2200c2d","compact":"b40b2acb186f7009a94dff5ad3865f4ffd160a5c939a74ee77f08a67247d10ac","nasal":"b40b2acb186f7009a94dff5ad3865f4ffd160a5c939a74ee77f08a67247d10ac"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-101-29","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":101,"verse":29,"english":"Having acquired the appellation of Satakratu, the sovereign of the celestials has gone to heaven; and, having performed rigid austerities, the Maharșis have attained the celestial regions.'","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.859,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-109-28"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2101029","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"0e23c43ac035d4f0d5b8e891efa6df7db32416bbc4406c297cf1c4ac863d85e2","compact":"20daeb0e5b33c5caa9711193657e42997319f956760c4b05a971f02f16983109","nasal":"20daeb0e5b33c5caa9711193657e42997319f956760c4b05a971f02f16983109"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-101-30","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":101,"verse":30,"english":"Truth, righteousness, prowess, kindness to creatures, fair spokeness, and worship of the twice-born ones, gods and guests, these have by the pious been styled the ways to heaven.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.898,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-109-30"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2101030","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"73fda3b1e355df8f98ce9186289fad99ce8307653f1f413f0ef6c12295bba873","compact":"97436f56d09a8011bd891a0ab830ec57a5cca373d139e1c332a1551b2ea785b2","nasal":"d84ae8d41e5e8eb995fa83d6ec29e4245a96f38fe76a3091db12e6eece6a422c"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-101-31","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":101,"verse":31,"english":"Therefore those Brahmanas, a men, who have spared life and in other ways practised morality, and have also given away in charity, performed austerities and served others, (perform sacrifices in consonance with Vedas). And principal ascetics engaged in religion, surrounded by the good, possessed of energy, having charity for their foremost attribute, void of envy, and their hearts free from all stain, are honoured in this world.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-109-35"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2101031","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"ad64d3572b0a6eb152b6beb4c2cd59d66713b847d6453707753e11315e850bf6","compact":"a321c9fe18e968d39a4270f1ef0911f770b252446b1966bc4a503864e1992b37","nasal":"bcaeff96ce9aab070baba2d4c14c022734a1185d3ba71b830333e96430c5abd7"}}]
